{
  "name": "caterpillar",
  "_about": "A monarch caterpillar (Danaus plexippus), 4.5 cm long: a plump smooth tube ringed black, yellow and white on every segment; a small round head striped the same; three pairs of short black true legs behind it, four pairs of stubby prolegs mid-body and a pair at the tail end; two long black filaments at the front and a shorter two at the back. It crawls by a wave running forward along its prolegs. Coats: the large white's caterpillar (grey-green speckled, a yellow line along its back and sides) and the swallowtail's (green, each segment banded black spotted orange). Written whole by tools/creaturegen/rework/insects/soft.py on insectlib.py (one smooth body on a chain of bones that ripples as it crawls).",
